; Logic capture for the PiLyzer.
;
; One state machine samples the eight inputs once per clock and pushes them
; four at a time, so the DMA moves whole words and a byte in memory is one
; sample. A second state machine watches the trigger pin at full speed and
; raises a flag: at 150 MS/s nothing running on the processor could see an edge
; in time, but the processor does not need to — it finds the exact edge in the
; captured data afterwards, so the trigger lands on a sample, not on an
; interrupt latency.

.program logic_capture
.wrap_target
    in pins, 8
.wrap

.program logic_trigger
public rise:
    wait 0 pin 0
    wait 1 pin 0
    jmp fire
public fall:
    wait 1 pin 0
    wait 0 pin 0
fire:
    irq nowait 4
stall:
    jmp stall
